    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d372">

                <pb facs="1432" n="1274" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1274"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Meyer to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-01-04"><hi rendition="#italic">January 4,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 391.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose, for the
                    information of the department, the French text<anchor n="a" xml:id="d372-f1"/>
                    of an imperial ukase dated the 14/27 of December, 1905, providing that in case
                    of mutinies or strikes on Russian railroads the managers of the lines may
                    proclaim martial law over all the property belonging to their division, and
                    enacting measures for enforcing this provision.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. von L. Meyer.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
